# Expert voice

Write as a specific working scientist setting a qualifying-exam item. The reader should not be able to tell a model helped.

Do

- Open on the physical/chemical/biological system and the given data
- Use field-native notation and a Methods-section tone for conventions
- Keep one or two slightly uneven sentences; do not polish every paragraph to the same length
- Put values in ranges an experimentalist would actually write down
- Name the asked object once, at the end of the prompt

Do not

- "In this problem we will", "it is important to note", "delve", "tapestry", "leverage", "robust", "pivotal", "comprehensive", "firstly/secondly", "as we all know", "trivially", "this demonstrates the power of"
- Define words a first-year graduate student already knows
- Clone the skeleton of `docs/examples/gold-harned-cell/task.md` or of the previous draft in this repo
- Write three stacked "and" lists in the prompt
- Cheer, hedge-stack, or tutor ("remember that")

If `check_voice.py` flags a phrase, rewrite the sentence from scratch.
